# Render's static sites do NOT read this Netlify-style file at all — confirmed
# empirically, not just in docs: sitemap/robots redirect rules added here had
# zero effect live even after removing a static file that would otherwise have
# shadowed them at the same path. The `routes` list in ../../render.yaml (a
# `type: redirect`/`type: rewrite` array) is the only mechanism Render's static
# sites actually read for this. This file is kept only for the one rule Render
# *does* apply automatically for a Vite SPA regardless (client-side routing
# still works without it), and as a historical note so nobody re-adds rules
# here expecting them to take effect.
/*    /index.html   200
